1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
They called the fire engine. A whale came. Around here, the fire engine is a whale.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,300
The lighthouse is dark and the boat is gone. Even the pebble has gone dim.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,900
Kong fixes his cap. Three postcards come out of his cheek.

4
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,500
This is the pelican mailbox. Letters ride next to the fish.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:12,500
The night delivery takes off.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,100
They waited while the moon crossed the whole sky. Mochi dozed a little.

7
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,900
Headlights. The turtle truck is a little slower than a walking seagull.

8
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,500
Mu and the conductor step out of the back. They got the postcards.

9
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,900
The crab family came too. Sideways, so it took a small detour.

10
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,500
Mochi runs in for a hug. The pebble glows bright again.

11
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,100
Battle plan. The spiral shell is the lighthouse, the clam is the boat, the stone is the whale.

12
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,700
Step one. The lighthouse keeper lives in the glass jar village. Off duty, he sleeps deeply.

13
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,900
Knocking doesn't wake him. Neither does the ticket punch.

14
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:35,500
Mu opens the lunchbox. The nose wakes up first.

15
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,100
But the watch points at the moon. It is off-duty time.

16
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,700
The conductor punches an overtime permit. Click.

17
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,100
With the right paperwork, he works. The keeper puts on his cap.

18
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:45,700
The jars light up one by one. The whole crew is on overtime.

19
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,500
A road of light appears on the sea. From the pier to the horizon.

20
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:51,100
Step two. The crabs click their claws. The seashell makes it loud.

21
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,700
An answer comes. It is the whale fireboat.

22
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:56,300
The conductor punches a third hole in the parcel. Now it is a boarding pass.

23
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,900
Mu packs him a fish lunch. The baby crab is already crying.

24
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,300
They climb onto the whale's back and follow the road of light.

25
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,100
A ladle, a punch and many claws wave goodbye. The second sun rises.

26
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:06,700
At the end of the road of light, the boat's lamp. Behind it, storm clouds.

27
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:10,700
The wind rises. The road of light breaks. (To be continued)

